#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: rozum-ucc-chat
version: 2.0.0
description: rozum UCC — chat app that drives a coding agent on the local model. Compiled to chat.html.
---
# rozum — chat (agent + model)

A phone-first CHAT app that drives a coding agent (claude/codex/opencode) on the LOCAL model over a
project. Each message runs the agent HEADLESS and non-interactively — `claude -p "<message>"` etc. via
`POST /control/session`-free `/control/coder/launch` — the exact reliable path the matrix scores 18/18
with. (v1 drove the interactive tmux REPL via send-keys, which wedged: Claude Code treats a
send-keys `Enter` as a newline, so messages piled up unsent — the "echo camera" bug. Headless has no
REPL/PTY to wedge.)

Flow: pick agent + model + project once (▶ chat) → then every message spawns a coder run
(`verify:false` — a chat turn is not a cargo task) → its log streams back as the assistant's answer.
The agent runs IN the project, so it can read + edit files + run commands to actually do the work.

Backend contract (same-origin, control-serve :8411, Face-ID-gated):
- `POST /control/coder/launch  {agent, model, workdir, prompt, verify:false}` → `{id, …}`
- `GET  /control/coder/log?id=&tail=` → `{id, alive, log}`
- `POST /control/coder/stop     {id}`
- `GET  /control/status` → `{installed:[{spec}], projects:[{name,path}], …}`

Compiled via: ssc run chat.ssc → chat.html  (see deploy-ucc-web.sh)

## Page
```scalascript
